# Cargo build artifacts.
/target

# `Cargo.lock` is intentionally COMMITTED.
#
# This workspace produces binaries (a client, and a server crate later), so the
# lockfile pins the exact resolution of GPUI's very large transitive tree. A
# git dependency already pins GPUI itself via `rev`, but its ~700 transitive
# crates would otherwise float on every build, and upstream Zed bumps them
# daily. Committing `Cargo.lock` is the standard Cargo guidance for
# applications and is what makes a clean checkout reproducible -- which is
# precisely what PLAN.md section 8 Phase 0 asks for ("a window opens on Windows
# from a clean checkout").
#
# A future `sh_nexus_wire`/`sh_nexus_server` library split would move the
# question to per-crate lockfiles; not a Phase 0 concern.

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
*.orig
*.rej

# Editor / IDE state.
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.template.json
*.code-workspace

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL-ONLY DEVELOPMENT ARTIFACTS
#
# Working documents that exist to drive development and are of no use to a
# reader of the repository. They are machine-local by design: the authoritative
# record of a decision is the ADR in docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, not the scratch file
# that produced it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Organic Driven Development task state (`odd/tasks/<feature>.md` and the
# Engram mirror under `odd/<feature>/`). This is the orchestrator's working
# checklist, rewritten on every task. The durable output of that work is the
# code, its tests, and the ADRs.
odd/

# Spec-Driven Development artifacts. `openspec/` is the file-based SDD store;
# Engram is the default store and lives outside the repository entirely, so it
# needs no rule here. A change's specs and designs are summarised into
# docs/ARCHITECTURE.md before a change is considered done.
openspec/
.sdd/
specs/
.specs/

# Agent scratch and per-machine agent configuration. Any `*.local.md` is a
# per-machine override of a versioned file of the same name, so the shared
# version stays the committed default.
.opencode/
.claude/
.cursor/
*.local.md
*.local
.local/

# Session notes, scratch and working capture. Never part of the deliverable.
notes/
scratch/
journal/
tmp/
*.notes.md
TODO.local.md
BRAINSTORM.local.md

# Coverage and profiling output. `cargo tarpaulin` and `cargo flamegraph` write
# these into the working directory; they are regenerated, never reviewed.
*.profraw
*.profdata
lcov.info
lcov-report/
tarpaulin-report.html
cobertura.xml
coverage.xml
coverage/
flamegraph.svg
*.flamegraph.svg
perf.data*

# CodeGraph's local index. A machine-local SQLite knowledge graph of the
# workspace that `gentle-ai codegraph init` writes into the project root. It is
# regenerated from the source on demand and is specific to this checkout, so it
# is disposable exactly like `target/`.
.codegraph/

# Locally generated test data. AGENTS.md section 8.2 requires large message
# histories to come from proptest generators rather than checked-in files, so
# anything produced by a generator run is disposable.
#
# NOTE: `crates/*/tests/fixtures/` is deliberately NOT ignored. AGENTS.md
# section 8.2 requires a real fixture set there (valid + invalid theme JSON, a
# recorded WebSocket session as JSONL, message payloads per protocol version).
# The generator output is ignored; the committed fixtures are not.
generated/
**/generated-testdata/

# Local development databases. Scoped to known dev locations so this cannot
# accidentally swallow the committed fixture databases under tests/fixtures/.
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
/sh_nexus.db*
/*.db
/*.db-shm
/*.db-wal
/data/
/var/
!crates/*/tests/fixtures/

# Secrets and local environment. Never commit these; the token store belongs in
# the OS keychain behind the `platform/` abstraction (AGENTS.md section 7.1).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!tests/fixtures/**/*.pem
secrets/
credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED
#
# These are the repository's actual documentation and they stay tracked:
#   README.md              entry point, prerequisites, platform gotchas
#   AGENTS.md              the project constitution; AGENTS.md sections 5.1,
#                          5.3 and 12 reference it for the QA and review
#                          process, so a clone without it cannot reproduce CI
#   PLAN.md                the implementation plan and the Phase 0 evidence
#   docs/ARCHITECTURE.md   the ADRs; the durable record of every decision
#   docs/DEPENDENCIES.md   the section 7.2 dependency audit
#   docs/API.md            the wire protocol and version negotiation
#
# Note that ignoring any of them now would not remove them from history: they
# are already pushed. Gitignore affects future adds only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
